      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SINABUN (8) made an encouraging start in Queensland when finishing a head away in second at this circuit and distance. That was his first outing for seven months and he generally goes well second-up so should be improved. Can win if things go his way from the back row. IM BOO NZ (2) was far from disgraced from the second line last start, finishing fifth. Led from this barrier to win the last time he started on the front row here three back. He should go forward again and could be hard to catch. GREATGREAT BOULDER (5) draws wider but is worth thought off a last-start win when he led and kept going to salute by 5 metres at Redcliffe. STUDLEIGH MARK (3) may be competitive from a good draw.",
